# Couchmode does not handle credentials.
# It spawns your agent's CLI, which uses the login that CLI already has
# (e.g. you ran `claude /login`, `codex login`, or the Gemini OAuth flow earlier).
#
# The variables below are OPTIONAL pass-throughs for people who prefer API keys,
# or who run on a machine with no stored CLI login. Couchmode never reads,
# logs, stores, or forwards their values - it only passes the ambient
# environment through to the agent process.

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
#
# A word of warning about these: an agent CLI generally prefers an API key over
# a stored login. An invalid or stale key in your shell profile will therefore
# break an agent that would otherwise work. If an agent reports an auth error
# while its CLI seems logged in, check for a leftover key in your environment
# before suspecting Couchmode.
